**Tests** — `tests/test_e2b.py` (27), `tests/test_e2b_scoring.py` (15), `tests/test_e2b_cost.py` (10)

## Cost (computed from the `runs-e2` ledger, not asserted)

54 shards, 108,000 records, 26,379,912 output tokens, **1.2435 GPU-hours**. Qwen alone 0.6244. Nine shards per model per language: 7 coupled caps + 2 decoupled, the announced-2048 cell shared. **Upper bound** — priced at v0 token totals; v1 shortens traces, so the real bill is lower. Not scaled down, because scaling 108,000 records by 3,000 pilot records would be inventing a number.

## The family as it stands

Unchanged: four cells (NATIVE × {de,th}, TRANSLATE-ACT × {de,th}), same estimand, announced {128, 2048} at `B* = 2048`, Holm α = 0.05 / α₁ = 0.0125. Scored **twice**, once per instrument; Holm runs within an instrument, never pooled to eight. NATIVE is the same `runs-e2` records in both columns, labelled `reused_from_e2` and asserted identical. Every emitted row carries `instrument`, `ledger` and a gate reading; v0 TRANSLATE-ACT rows carry an inline uninformative-null warning. §8.3's remove-never-add rule stands: a passing Swahili cell still does not enter the family.

## What I think is wrong

